---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FeedList from '../../components/FeedList.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const raw = (await getCollection('matchaAnalytics')).sort((a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf());
const entries = await Promise.all(
  raw.map(async (e) => ({ slug: e.slug, data: e.data, Content: (await e.render()).Content }))
);
---
<BaseLayout title="Matcha Analytics" description="Tracking matcha consumption and how my views shift across variants.">
  <div class="prose" style="padding-top:2.5rem;">
    <h1>Matcha Analytics</h1>
    <p style="color:var(--text-muted)">
      When I was in NYC with Paige, she Matcha for the first time and didn't really like it. Once I had ~1/2 of mine, she gave me the rest of hers, so I had a large surplus of Matcha.I was initially planning on meeting a friend later, so I set aside the rest of the matcha to give her since I had already had enough. That hangout did not end up happening, and so I had extra matcha that was now warm while I was on the train home. I always get my drinks cold, and have for a long time, so I thought this would be worse, but when I drank it, I actually found it to be much more flavorful. This was a reminder to never rely too heavily on heuristic thinking and always re-evaluate the mechanisms you use to make decisions.
      In this vein I've decided to meticulously document all of my matcha consumption to eventually locate my favorite one, both towards a practical goal and as an excersize in thoughtfulness.
    </p>
    <FeedList entries={entries} pdfDir="matcha-files" emptyMessage="Nothing here yet — add a Markdown file to src/content/matchaAnalytics/ to get started." />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
